      text: `<p></p> <p>Consider the following relational schema:</p> <p> \\( \\text{Suppliers}(\\underline{\\text{sid:integer}},\\text{ sname:string, city:string, street:string}) \\) &nbsp; </p> <p> \\( \\text{Parts}(\\underline{\\text{pid:integer}}, \\text{ pname:string, color:string}) \\) &nbsp; </p> <p> \\( \\text{Catalog}(\\underline {\\text{sid:integer, pid:integer}}, \\text{cost:real}) \\) </p> <p>Consider the following relational query on the above database:</p> <pre data-pbcklang="sql" data-pbcktabsize="4" class="prettyprint linenums lang-sql prettyprinted" style=""><ol class="linenums"><li class="L0"><span class="pln">SELECT	S</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">sname</span></li><li class="L1"><span class="pln">FROM    </span><span class="typ">Suppliers</span><span class="pln"> S</span></li><li class="L2"><span class="pln">WHERE S</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">sid NOT IN </span><span class="pun">(</span><span class="pln">SELECT C</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">sid </span></li><li class="L3"><span class="pln">                    FROM </span><span class="typ">Catalog</span><span class="pln"> C </span></li><li class="L4"><span class="pln">                    WHERE C</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">pid NOT IN </span><span class="pun">(</span><span class="pln">SELECT P</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">pid </span></li><li class="L5"><span class="pln">                                        FROM </span><span class="typ">Parts</span><span class="pln"> P </span></li><li class="L6"><span class="pln">                                        WHERE P</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">color</span><span class="pun">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="str">'blue'</span><span class="pun">))</span></li></ol></pre> <p>Assume that relations corresponding to the above schema are not empty. Which one of the following is the correct interpretation of the above query?</p> <p></p>`,
