      text: `<p></p> <p>Suppose physical memory can store  \\( \\mathbf{N} \\) pages, and our demand paging system uses an LRU (Least Recently Used) replacement policy. If a process's resident set contains (  \\( \\mathbf{N + 1} \\) ) distinct pages that are accessed sequentially forever, i.e.,<br> \$\$  P_{1}, P_{2}, \\ldots, P_{N}, P_{N+1}, P_{1}, P_{2}, \\ldots  \$\$ <br>what will be the hit rate of this demand paging system?<br>&nbsp; </p> <p></p>`,
